### NDIS Reporting Requirements in South Australia

#### **1. Restrictive Practices Authorisation Scheme**
- **Written Notices**: NDIS service providers must report the use of Level 1 and Level 2 authorised restrictive practices. This includes providing written notices to the individual with a disability, their guardian, or substitute decision-maker [1](https://www.sa.gov.au/topics/care-and-support/disability/restrictive-practices/ndis-service-providers/reporting-obligations).
- **Twice-Yearly Reporting**: Providers must report to the Restrictive Practices Unit about the authorisation of Level 1 restrictive practices twice a year (30 June and 31 December) [1](https://www.sa.gov.au/topics/care-and-support/disability/restrictive-practices/ndis-service-providers/reporting-obligations).

#### **2. NDIS Quality and Safeguards Commission**
- **Reportable Incidents**: Providers must notify the Commission of reportable incidents, including the use of unauthorised restrictive practices, serious injuries, abuse, neglect, and deaths [2](https://www.ndiscommission.gov.au/rules-and-standards/managing-and-reporting-incidents/reportable-incidents).
- **Incident Management System**: Providers must have an incident management system in place to record, respond to, and manage incidents [2](https://www.ndiscommission.gov.au/rules-and-standards/managing-and-reporting-incidents/reportable-incidents).

#### **3. Additional Reporting Requirements**
- **Behaviour Support Plans**: Providers must develop and report on behaviour support plans for individuals requiring restrictive practices[1](https://www.sa.gov.au/topics/care-and-support/disability/restrictive-practices/ndis-service-providers/reporting-obligations).
- **Training and Compliance**: Providers must report on staff training and compliance with NDIS standards and guidelines[1](https://www.sa.gov.au/topics/care-and-support/disability/restrictive-practices/ndis-service-providers/reporting-obligations).

These requirements ensure transparency, accountability, and the safety and well-being of individuals receiving NDIS services in South Australia.

